+++ b/docs/content/archive.md
@@ -152,6 +152,25 @@ $ rclone copy -vv :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip /tmp/100files
 ...
 ```
 
+## Symlinks
+
+Any symbolic links in a Zip or Squashfs archive are skipped unless the
+`--links` / `-l` flag is in use.
+
+With `--links` a symlink is exposed as a file with the `.rclonelink`
+suffix, whose size is the length of the link target and whose contents
+are the link target. This means `rclone copy --links` will recreate the
+symlink on a backend which supports them, e.g.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip
+        5 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Oct 27 14:39 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
 ## Zip
 
 The [Zip file format](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZIP_(file_format))
